ncumbent Stephanie Bice (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Oklahoma's 5th District leans Republican by about nine points, and Republican Stephanie Bice is seeking reelection with a large financial advantage. She has raised roughly $2.4 million and holds $1.7 million on hand, while Democrat Jena Nelson, the 2022 education nominee, has raised about $740,000. Most race raters call the district solidly or safely Republican, and prediction markets give Nelson roughly a one-in-eight chance of winning.\n\nStill, there are signs of a competitive undercard. A September poll from a Democratic-leaning firm showed Bice ahead by only five points, and national Democrats have added the seat to their target list, an unusual step in Oklahoma. Bice has declined debates so far while announcing $2.7 million in federal project funding for the district. The forecast expects Bice to win by high single digits, with Nelson needing an unusually strong national environment to close the gap.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0558, "margin": -10.29}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0638, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.1454, "margin": -7.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0909, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.1152, "margin": -7.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0488, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.099, "margin": -8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.1151, "margin": -8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0881, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.0678, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.0911, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.0833, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.097, "margin": -8.8}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.0712, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.0816, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.0827, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.0573, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.0